    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="0761" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/9–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Syria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Porter</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Damascus</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-28T18:00:00+02:00">September 28,
                            1945—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 29—2:16 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>64. Rising press and public sentiment resulting from sensational treatment
                    accorded by British controlled press and radio in Near <pb facs="0762" n="750"
                        xml:id="pg750"/> East to alleged letter of President Truman to Mr. Attlee
                    advocating 100,000 Jewish immigrants for Palestine leads me to inquire whether
                    Department contemplates issuance of mitigating statement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Porter</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
